    <p>
      By booking, paying for, accepting delivery of, or using a Ridgeway Rentals dump
      trailer, the customer (“Renter”) agrees to the following Terms &amp; Conditions.
    </p>

    <h2>1. RENTAL PERIOD</h2>
    <p>
      The standard rental fee includes <strong>up to seven (7) days</strong> from the date 
      of delivery.
    </p>

    <p>
      If the trailer is required for longer than seven (7) days, additional rental time 
      is charged at <strong>$50.00</strong> per day, subject to trailer availability.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter must contact Ridgeway Rentals before the end of the rental period if
      additional time is required. Extensions are not guaranteed and are subject to
      availability.
    </p>

    <h2>2. INCLUDED WEIGHT &amp; OVERWEIGHT CHARGES</h2>
    <p>
      The rental fee includes disposal of up to <strong>500 kg</strong> of material.
    </p>

    <p>
      Any disposal weight exceeding the included 500 kg allowance will be charged at:
      <strong>$2 per additional kilogram</strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      The disposal facility's measured weight will be used to determine the total disposal
      weight where applicable.
    </p>    

    <p>
        The Renter is responsible for all overweight charges associated with materials
        placed in the trailer.
    </p>

    <h2>3. DELIVERY &amp; TRAILER PLACEMENT</h2>
    <p>
      The Renter is responsible for providing a safe, firm, level, and accessible location
      for delivery and pickup of the trailer.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter authorizes Ridgeway Rentals and its representatives to enter the
      property as reasonably necessary to deliver and retrieve the trailer.
    </p>

    <p>
      Ridgeway Rentals will make reasonable efforts to place the trailer in the Renter's
      requested location; however, the driver has final discretion regarding placement
      based on safety, accessibility, ground conditions, overhead clearances, and the
      ability to safely retrieve the loaded trailer.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter is responsible for ensuring that the requested placement area can
      support the weight of the trailer and its contents.
    </p>

    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, Ridgeway Rentals is not responsible for damage to
      driveways, asphalt, concrete, interlocking stone, curbs, lawns, landscaping,
      underground services, septic systems, irrigation systems, or other property
      resulting from the normal placement, loading, or removal of the trailer, except
      where caused by Ridgeway Rentals' negligence.
    </p>

    <h2>4. LOADING REQUIREMENTS</h2>
    <p>
      All materials must remain <strong>completely inside the trailer.</strong><br/>
      Nothing may extend above the top edge of the trailer or hang over the sides, front,
      or rear.
    </p>

    <p>
      The load must be reasonably level and evenly distributed.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter must not concentrate excessive weight in one area of the trailer.
    </p>

    <p>
      The trailer doors must be able to completely close and securely latch before pickup.
    </p>

    <p>
      Ridgeway Rentals may refuse to transport any trailer that is overloaded, improperly
      loaded, unsafe, or not compliant with these Terms &amp; Conditions.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter will be required to remove or redistribute material before pickup if
      Ridgeway Rentals determines that the trailer cannot be safely or legally
      transported.
    </p>

    <h2>5. CONCRETE, SOIL, SHINGLES &amp; HEAVY MATERIALS</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Ridgeway Rentals must be notified BEFORE any concrete, soil, dirt, roofing
        shingles, or similar heavy material is placed in the trailer. Failure to do so may
        result in additional fees or refusal of service.
      </strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      Concrete, soil/dirt, and shingles must be <strong>kept separate from other waste
      materials</strong> and may not be mixed together or mixed with general household or
      construction waste unless specifically approved by Ridgeway Rentals.
    </p>

    <p>
      Heavy materials are subject to specific loading limits due to trailer payload and
      legal transportation weight restrictions.
    </p>

    <p>
      Ridgeway Rentals will advise the Renter of the allowable quantity or fill level
      before loading begins.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter must follow all loading instructions provided by Ridgeway Rentals.<br/>
      Failure to notify Ridgeway Rentals or failure to properly separate these materials
      may result in additional disposal charges, unloading requirements, a failed pickup
      charge, and/or other applicable fees.
    </p>

    <h2 id="prohibited-items">6. PROHIBITED ITEMS &amp; MATERIALS</h2>
    <p>
      The following items are <strong>STRICTLY PROHIBITED</strong> and must NOT be placed 
      in a Ridgeway Rentals trailer:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Tires of any kind</strong></li>
      <li>Asbestos or asbestos-containing materials</li>
      <li>Hazardous waste or hazardous materials</li>
      <li>Gasoline, diesel fuel, kerosene, or other fuels</li>
      <li>Propane tanks or cylinders</li>
      <li>Compressed gas cylinders</li>
      <li>Oxygen tanks</li>
      <li>Paint, paint thinner, stains, varnishes, or solvents</li>
      <li>Motor oil or other automotive fluids</li>
      <li>Antifreeze</li>
      <li>Pesticides and herbicides</li>
      <li>Industrial or hazardous chemicals</li>
      <li>Flammable materials</li>
      <li>Explosive materials</li>
      <li>Fireworks</li>
      <li>Ammunition or explosive devices</li>
      <li>Automotive, lithium, industrial, or other hazardous batteries</li>
      <li>Medical or biomedical waste</li>
      <li>Needles or syringes</li>
      <li>Pharmaceutical waste</li>
      <li>Radioactive materials</li>
      <li>Contaminated soil</li>
      <li>Sewage or human waste</li>
      <li>Animal waste in bulk quantities</li>
      <li>Biohazardous materials</li>
      <li>Liquid waste of any kind</li>
      <li>Hot ashes or hot coals</li>
      <li>Burning or smoldering materials</li>
      <li>Dead animals or animal carcasses</li>
      <li>Any illegal substances or materials</li>
      <li>Any material prohibited by the receiving disposal facility</li>
      <li>Any material prohibited by applicable municipal, provincial, or federal laws</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      <strong>
        If you are unsure whether an item is permitted, contact Ridgeway Rentals BEFORE 
        placing it in the trailer.
      </strong>
    </p>

    <h2>7. PROHIBITED ITEM FEE</h2>
    <p>
      A <strong>minimum prohibited item fee of $200.00</strong> will apply if prohibited 
      materials are placed in the trailer.
    </p>

    <p>
      The $200 prohibited item fee is <strong>in addition to</strong> any actual costs incurred by
      Ridgeway Rentals for handling, removing, transporting, returning, cleaning, or
      properly disposing of the prohibited material.
    </p>

    <p>
      If a disposal facility rejects a load because prohibited materials are present, the
      Renter will be responsible for applicable additional costs and fees.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter is responsible for everything placed in the trailer during the rental
      period, including materials placed in the trailer by neighbours, contractors,
      members of the public, or any other third party.
    </p>

    <h2>8. FAILED PICKUP FEE</h2>
    <p>
      A <strong>$50.00 failed pickup fee</strong> may be charged when Ridgeway Rentals 
      arrives for a scheduled pickup and is unable to safely retrieve the trailer due to 
      circumstances within the Renter's control, including:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Blocked access to the trailer</li>
      <li>Vehicles or equipment preventing pickup</li>
      <li>Gates being locked or inaccessible</li>
      <li>Trailer being overloaded</li>
      <li>Materials extending above or outside the trailer</li>
      <li>Improperly distributed loads</li>
      <li>Trailer doors being unable to close</li>
      <li>Prohibited materials being present</li>
      <li>Heavy materials being loaded contrary to Ridgeway Rentals' instructions</li>
      <li>Unsafe site conditions that should reasonably have been addressed by the Renter</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The Renter must correct the issue before another pickup attempt is made.
    </p>

    <h2>9. TRAILER USE</h2>

    <p>
      The trailer is provided for waste and debris collection only.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter must NOT:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Move, tow, relocate, or reposition the trailer.</li>
      <li>Permit another person or company to move or tow the trailer.</li>
      <li>Allow children to enter or play in or around the trailer.</li>
      <li>Climb on the trailer.</li>
      <li>Burn materials inside the trailer.</li>
      <li>Modify, drill, weld, paint, or otherwise alter the trailer.</li>
      <li>Use machinery to compact materials inside the trailer without written approval.</li>
      <li>Load the trailer in a manner that could damage the trailer or create an unsafe condition.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Only Ridgeway Rentals or an authorized representative may move or tow the trailer.
    </p>

    <h2>10. CUSTOMER RESPONSIBILITY</h2>

    <p>
      The Renter is responsible for the trailer and its contents while the trailer is 
      located at the delivery address.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter should take reasonable precautions to prevent unauthorized use,
      vandalism, or other persons from placing prohibited materials in the trailer.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Renter is responsible for obtaining any required permits, parking permissions,
      municipal approvals, condominium approvals, or property-owner authorization
      required for placement of the trailer.
    </p>

    <h2>11. DAMAGE TO THE TRAILER</h2>

    <p>
      The Renter may be responsible for repair or replacement costs for damage caused
      by misuse, overloading, improper loading, unauthorized movement, prohibited
      materials, fire, or other damage caused by the Renter or persons using the trailer
      with the Renter's permission.
    </p>

    <p>
      Normal wear and tear is excluded.
    </p>

    <h2>12. ACCESS FOR PICKUP</h2>

    <p>
      The Renter must provide Ridgeway Rentals with clear and safe access to the trailer
      on the scheduled pickup date.
    </p>

    <p>
      Vehicles, equipment, construction materials, snow, gates, or other obstructions
      must not prevent Ridgeway Rentals from safely retrieving the trailer.
    </p>

    <p>
      Additional charges may apply if a return trip is required.
    </p>

    <h2>13. SUMMARY OF STANDARD FEES</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>Fee:</strong> $395.00<br>
      <strong>Standard Rental Period:</strong> Up to 7 days<br>
      <strong>If additional dump trip required within the 7 days:</strong> $250.00 additional fee<br>
      <strong>Included Disposal Weight:</strong> 500 kg<br>
      <strong>Additional Weight:</strong> $2.00/kg over 500 kg<br>
      <strong>Additional Rental Days:</strong> $50.00/day<br>
      <strong>Failed Pickup Fee:</strong> $50.00<br>
      <strong>Prohibited Item Fee:</strong> Minimum $200.00, plus any additional handling or disposal costs
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Tires:</strong> NOT PERMITTED
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Concrete / Soil / Dirt / Shingles:</strong> Ridgeway Rentals must be 
      notified in advance.<br/>
      These materials must be separated and loaded according to Ridgeway Rentals' instructions.
    </p>

    <p>
      Applicable taxes will be added to fees where required.
    </p>

    <h2>14. WEATHER</h2>

    <p>
      The Renter is responsible for taking reasonable precautions to protect the trailer
      and its contents from weather conditions where appropriate.
    </p>

    <p>
      Rain, snow, ice, and water accumulation can increase the weight of materials in the
      trailer. The Renter remains responsible for disposal weight exceeding the included
      500 kg allowance.
    </p>

    <h2>15. RIGHT TO REFUSE TRANSPORTATION</h2>
    <p>
      Ridgeway Rentals reserves the right to delay or refuse pickup if the trailer is:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Overloaded</li>
      <li>Improperly loaded</li>
      <li>Unsafe to transport</li>
      <li>Inaccessible</li>
      <li>Loaded with prohibited materials</li>
      <li>Loaded contrary to Ridgeway Rentals' instructions</li>
      <li>Otherwise, unable to be legally or safely transported</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>16. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY</h2>

    <p>
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, Ridgeway Rentals is not responsible for
      indirect or consequential losses resulting from the rental or use of the trailer
      including any damage to the driveway.
    </p>

    <p>
      Nothing in these Terms &amp; Conditions is intended to exclude or limit any rights or
      liabilities that cannot legally be excluded or limited under applicable Ontario law.
    </p>

    <h2>17. ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS</h2>

    <p>
      By booking a trailer, making payment, signing a rental agreement, or accepting
      delivery of a Ridgeway Rentals trailer, the Renter confirms that they have read,
